(MASTER SUPPLY AGREEMENT - MSA-SUP-105) '
(Between: Contoso Manufacturing Holdings \("Buyer"\) and STARK INDUSTRIAL \("Supplier"\), Supplier) '
(ID SUP-105.) '
(Supplier region: AMER. Supplier tier: TIER_1. Effective Date: 1 January 2025. Term: 36 months.) '
() '
(1. Definitions) '
(1.1 "Promised Date" means the delivery date stated on the purchase order.) '
(1.2 "Financial Exposure" means the invoice value \(quantity multiplied by unit price\) of Late) '
(Deliveries plus documented unplanned production downtime cost attributable to Supplier. Planned) '
(maintenance downtime is excluded.) '
() '
(2. Scope. Supplier shall supply components to Buyer plants in AMER, EMEA and APAC per issued) '
(purchase orders.) '
() '
(3. Pricing. Prices are fixed per the price schedule; changes require 90 days written notice.) '
() '
(4. Quality. Supplier shall maintain ISO 9001 certification and a defect rate below 500 PPM.) '
() '
(5. Delivery and Grace Period) '
(5.1 A delivery is a "Late Delivery" if received more than 2 calendar days after the Promised) '
(Date.) '
(5.2 Cancelled or undelivered purchase orders are not Late Deliveries for the purposes of) '
(Section 7.) '
() '
(6. Reporting. Supplier shall provide weekly delivery performance reports.) '
() '
(7. Liquidated Damages for Late Delivery) '
(7.1 Buyer may claim liquidated damages equal to 5.0% of Financial Exposure for the contract) '
(year.) '
() '
(8. Limitation of Liability) '
(8.1 Aggregate liquidated damages under Section 7 shall not exceed USD 500,000 per contract) '
(year.) '
() '
(9. Force Majeure) '
(9.1 Neither party is liable for delay caused by events beyond reasonable control, provided) '
(written notice is given within 5 business days.) '
(9.2 Force Majeure must be formally declared and acknowledged by both parties to apply.) '
(9.3 Declared Force Majeure Event. The parties acknowledge a declared Force Majeure Event:) '
(closure of the Port of Long Beach from 1 March 2025 to 31 March 2025. Purchase orders with a) '
(Promised Date within this period are excluded from Liquidated Damages under Section 7, and) '
(unplanned downtime occurring within this period shall not be attributed to Supplier.) '
() '
(10. Termination. Buyer may terminate for convenience with 60 days notice, or immediately if) '
(on-time delivery falls below 70% for two consecutive quarters.) '
() '
(11. Governing Law. This Agreement is governed by the laws of the State of Delaware.) '
() '
ET
endstream
